Below is the complete Terraform HCL program that sets up a DNS zone in Route 53 and creates an A record mapping a domain name to an IPv4 address. The program includes the necessary input variables with default values.

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"
}

variable "domain_name" {
  description = "The domain name for the Route 53 zone"
  default     = "example.com"
}

variable "ipv4_address" {
  description = "The IPv4 address to map in the A record"
  default     = "192.0.2.1"
}

resource "aws_route53_zone" "primary_zone" {
  name    = var.domain_name
  comment = "DNS zone for ${var.domain_name}"
}

resource "aws_route53_record" "a_record" {
  zone_id = aws_route53_zone.primary_zone.zone_id
  name    = var.domain_name
  type    = "A"
  ttl     = 300
  records = [var.ipv4_address]
}
```

This configuration does the following:
1. Configures the AWS provider to use the `us-east-1` region.
2. Defines two input variables: `domain_name` and `ipv4_address`, both with default values.
3. Creates a Route 53 DNS zone for the specified domain name.
4. Creates an A record within the DNS zone that maps the domain name to the specified IPv4 address. The TTL for the record is set to 300 seconds.

