1. An IAM role named `lightsail-instance-role` with the necessary trust relationship to be assumed by Lightsail.
2. An IAM policy attachment that attaches the `AmazonLightsailFullAccess` policy to the IAM role.
3. A Lightsail instance named `example-lightsail-instance` in the `us-east-1a` availability zone using the `amazon_linux_2` blueprint and `nano_1_0` bundle.
4. Two additional Lightsail disks named `additional-disk-1` and `additional-disk-2` with sizes of 20 GB and 30 GB respectively.
5. Disk attachments to mount the additional disks to the Lightsail instance at `/dev/xvdf` and `/dev/xvdg`.

Make sure to adjust the `availability_zone`, `blueprint_id`, and `bundle_id` if you need different configurations. The region is set to `us-east-1`, but you can change it to any other region where Lightsail is available.

